  "limitations": "MR-08 only; MR-09 through MR-17 and the complete goal remain unachieved. Native callbacks are trusted/cooperative, not OS sandboxed. Startup supplies current trusted topology/grant configuration: live grant revisions/tombstones do not independently persist operator policy; durable control-plane distribution and dynamic placement/directory lifecycles remain MR-11/MR-13/MR-17. Query-only bindings require existing registered namespace/birth metadata and explicit replica routing; they refuse commands/local reads/status. Four ignored execution/runtime/transport child entry points are invoked by parents and excluded from owning counts. Broad qualification uses the final production source; the last test-only change adds actual nonmember native/Axum HTTP coverage, followed by a full 22-case host run, targeted Clippy and format check. These loopback/same-machine fixtures do not establish physical power loss, zones, production capacity, S3 archive/restore, snapshots, automatic repair, effects or the remaining release/scaling gates. S3 commands remain refused before private work. Existing vendored warnings remain visible. Internal SDK placement/origin fields and query header changes are hard cutovers without old readers/conversion.",
